Description: fate/vvc: test base pictures and SEI in multilayer access units
 Decode the base pictures of VPS_A_3 and OPI_B_3, comparing against
 independent layer-0 extraction references. Enable crccheck+explode so
 allowing enhancement suffix SEI to overwrite a base picture's hash
 fails the tests, even when the output pixels would otherwise match.
 .
 Check content light level metadata with a generated sample containing
 1000/400 in layer 0 and 2000/800 in layer 1. Only the layer-0 message
 may reach the decoded pictures.
 .
 Signed-off-by: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
 Assisted-by: Claude Opus via Claude Code
 Assisted-by: GPT-6 via Codex
 .
 Port to 9.0.2: tests/fate/vvc.mak: the hunk lists are placed by 9.0.2 context (fate-vvc-eos-cra sits beside them).
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Origin: other, https://code.ffmpeg.org/danielcamposramos/FFmpeg/commit/edfce157285004d8311c4c60cd2419910f3a4f84
Forwarded: no, held by Daniel 2026-11-03 (fork branch vvc-layer-au on code.ffmpeg.org/danielcamposramos/FFmpeg)
